  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the HIV and TB Response in Egypt - Egypt (01-Apr-2019-31-Mar-2022)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Egypt, TB/HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Egypt Co)This program has the following goals: Strengthen Sustainable Responses to HIV in Egypt to achieve the International fast-track targets (90-90-90).  Strengthen the national response to TB to reduce the incidence and prevalence of TB including Multi-Drug Resistance (MD-R) TB. The objectives of this program are: Achieving the global target of HIV testing and diagnosis: Ensuring that 90% of PLHIV know their HIV status by 2022..  Achieving the global target on HIV treatment and care: Ensuring that 90% of PLHIV who know their status are on treatment..  Achieving the global target on Zero HIV new infections: Ensuring that the new HIV infections are reduced by 50% by 2022..  Expansion and scaling up successful interventions and introduce evidence based new technology and processes to improve case finding within identified key populations,.  Building strong, sustainable and resilient community and health services to deliver HIV services..  To detect 90% of estimated TB cases including among key-affected-populations  and successfully treat 90% of them by 2022..  To detect 85% of estimated MDR-TB patients and successfully treat 80% by 2022.  To strengthen TB surveillance , M&amp;E and program management including implementing comprehensive systems for data management, to meet the NSP targets</narrative>
  </description>
